@startuml selector
' ============================================================================
' Backend selector (1 of 2) — "which libdictenstein backend should I reach for?"
' This figure covers the SUBSTRING-search subtree (you answered YES to the top
' decision, "match substrings, not prefixes"). The PREFIX / WORD subtree — the
' other five backends — is the companion figure selector-2.puml.
' Color key:  green = always-on in-memory   amber = feature `pathmap-backend`
'             blue  = feature `persistent-artrie` (disk-backed)
'             pale-yellow = the (already-resolved) top decision
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 115
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #F9A825
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #37474F

title Choosing a libdictenstein backend — substring search (1 of 2)

start
:Store terms\n(optionally\nterm → value);
:Match **substrings**\n(not prefixes)? **→ yes**\n(prefix / word lookup:\nsee companion **selector-2**);<<#FFF9C4>>

if (Persist +\ncrash-safe?) then (yes)
  if (Compact /\n2-way index?) then (yes)
    :**Persistent**\n**Scdawg / …Char**\ncompact\nsuffix graph\n(snapshot rd,\nCOW wr);<<#BBDEFB>>
  else (suffix API)
    :**Persistent**\n**Suffix**\n**Automaton /**\n**Tree**\nbyte / Unicode;<<#BBDEFB>>
  endif
else (in-memory)
  if (Static\n(build once)?) then (yes)
    :**Scdawg / …Char**\ncompact\nsymmetric DAWG\n(2-way index);<<#C8E6C9>>
  else (mutable)
    :**Suffix**\n**Automaton**\n**(Char)**\n(<latex>\le 2 \cdot n - 1</latex>\nstates);<<#C8E6C9>>
  endif
endif
stop

legend bottom
| Color | Family |
|<#C8E6C9>| in-memory (always on) |
|<#FFF59D>| feature pathmap-backend |
|<#BBDEFB>| feature persistent-artrie (disk) |
|<#FFF9C4>| top decision (resolved) |
endlegend
@enduml
